      "problem": "Simplify the expression $(P∧Q)∧(P⇒¬Q).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's simplify the expression using the properties of logical operation\n\n- First, we use that $X⇒Y≡¬X∨Y:$\n\n$$\n(P∧Q)∧(P⇒¬Q)≡(P∧Q)∧(¬P∨¬Q)\n$$\n\n- Next, we use a De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n(P∧Q)∧(¬P∨¬Q)≡(P∧Q)∧¬(P∧Q)\n$$\n\n- Finally, we use the fact that the conjunction of a statement and its negation is a contradiction:\n\n$$\n(P∧Q)∧¬(P∧Q)≡c\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n(P∧Q)∧(P⇒¬Q)≡c.\n$$",
